        .title Academia

        a.sub-title(href="https://xrlab.berkeley.edu/research/bampfa-ar-the-hands-that-built-the-building/", target="_blank") BAMPFA AR - XR Lab
        .position Immersive Experience Designer and Developer  • 2018-Present
        .blurb As part of the XR Lab, I am building the Augmented Reality experience for the Berkeley Art Museum and Pacific Film Archive (BAMPFA), funded by the Arts+Design initiative. Working with Unity and ARKit, I am designing modern interactions, animations and data displays. In using AR to recognize the builders that constructed BAMPFA itself, our team also aims to push the boundaries of educational storytelling, and to show the efficacy of using new media to tell human stories.

        a.sub-title Immersive Cinema - VR@Berkeley
        .position Team Lead • 2016-Present
        .blurb We are a research and production group at UC Berkeley furthering the current language, body of knowledge, and defining the standards that describes 360 and immersive cinema.
